      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Redis gives all the things in the form string mostly\n- So we need a mechanism to convert the data type or property corresponding to redis\n    into java/springboot based property\n- client that is going to help us while implementing redis in spring boot application is gonna be jedis\n- Difference between jedis and Spring data starter data redis (this is internally going to use jedis only)\n- jedis is more bare metal, most jedis operations are blocking\n- Spring data starter redis gives redis template supports both non-blocking and blocking property\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Redis gives all the things in the form string mostly\n- So we need a mechanism to convert the data type or property corresponding to redis\n    into java/springboot based property\n- client that is going to help us while implementing redis in spring boot application is gonna be jedis\n- Difference between jedis and Spring data starter data redis (this is internally going to use jedis only)\n- jedis is more bare metal, most jedis operations are blocking\n- Spring data starter redis gives redis template supports both non-blocking and blocking property\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
